From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AbdelH2O <a.hana@aui.ma>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:16:07 +0000
Subject: ipn/ipnlocal: add ServeConfig stub for builds without serve

feature/acme calls LocalBackend.ServeConfig from its cert refresh loop,
but the ts_omit_serve stubs did not provide it, so a build that omits
serve and keeps ACME failed to compile:

    feature/acme/refresh.go:88:10: b.ServeConfig undefined

The acme feature does not depend on serve, so this combination should
build. Return an invalid view, which callers already treat as "no
serve config".

diff --git a/ipn/ipnlocal/serve_disabled.go b/ipn/ipnlocal/serve_disabled.go
index 7123ebe3bb112edd107e1cb96521cc57d9f94818..9c2d7e4cd5ddb194bfe0bd5d0dec6060d9da0cdf 100644
--- a/ipn/ipnlocal/serve_disabled.go
+++ b/ipn/ipnlocal/serve_disabled.go
@@ -32,6 +32,13 @@ func (*LocalBackend) HasFunnelForHostPort(host string, port uint16) bool {
 	return false
 }
 
+// ServeConfig returns an invalid view: there is no serve config in
+// builds without serve. Features that remain linked, such as
+// feature/acme, call it to find the hostnames served over HTTPS.
+func (b *LocalBackend) ServeConfig() ipn.ServeConfigView {
+	return ipn.ServeConfigView{}
+}
+
 func (b *LocalBackend) vipServicesFromPrefsLocked(prefs ipn.PrefsView) []*tailcfg.VIPService {
 	return nil
 }
